## ✅ 2. Rename Scripts with `.go` Extensions

### From GitHub:
1. Click on each filename (`block_tor_traffic`, etc.)
2. Click the pencil icon 🖉 (top right)
3. Rename to `block_tor_traffic.go`, then click **“Commit changes”**

Repeat for:
- `post_body_and_query_values.go`
- `pulling_usr_from_redacted_info.go`
- `tornode_tag_check.go`

---

## ✅ 3. Create a `.gitignore` for Go

Create a new file in the root of the repo:
- Name it `.gitignore`
- Paste the following into it:

```gitignore
# Go build artifacts
bin/
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test

# Output of `go coverage`
*.out

# IDE settings
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

